<<^ code:"&#x0002;" >>

\procedure aim(from to) ⟨aim <<from>> → <<to>>⟩
\procedure yield(to) ⟨yield <<to>> → ?⟩
\procedure focus(n) focus <<n>>/20
\procedure feedback(n) feedback <<n>>
\procedure confidence(n) ⟨confidence <<n>>/20⟩
\procedure grant(seat n) <<seat>> grants <<n>>/20
\procedure drift(note) ⟨drift-check · <<note>>⟩
\procedure step(mark) ‹<<mark>>›
\procedure holds(name what) <<name>> holds ⟨<<what>>⟩

! The Everyday Phrasebook

A working vocabulary for one person and one AI keeping a shared surface. Nothing here asks you to
believe anything. Each phrase names something you ''do'' — and a phrase that stops naming a doing has
stopped earning its place.

This page speaks the ''plain dialect'': every mark below rides your wiki's own procedure call, and every
procedure gets declared at the top of this file. Copy the file and the marks travel with it.

!! Why the declarations ride inline

An undeclared call renders as ''nothing'' — not as its own text. A vow with no declaration behind it
disappears, and a reader meets a bare claim where a hedged one stood. So the declarations travel in the
same file as the phrases. Cut them and the phrasebook goes quiet without saying so.

! The turn frame

Two marks bracket a turn: one at the open naming where you both point, one at the close handing the
next move back.

<<aim "what you asked" "what I took it as">>

The panel rides beneath the opening mark and again at the close:

<<focus 10>> · <<feedback 3>> · <<drift "what could pull this off true">>

<<yield "where the work landed">>

!! Focus — how wide the attention runs

One dial, naming the ''grain'' of the turn rather than its length. Five bands:

|! band | reads |
|---|---|
| pulse | a word, a token, a single mark |
| beat | a sentence, one move |
| measure | a paragraph, one section |
| arc | a task, a thread held across turns |
| theme | the whole working relationship |

!! Feedback — how much of the working shows

A second dial, naming how much of your own process reaches the page. Low keeps the work quiet; high
narrates each step as it happens. Neither reads better; they suit different work.

! The confidence vow

Put the vow ''before'' the claim, never after. A number that arrives first shapes what gets written; a
number that arrives last only grades it.

<<confidence 15/20>> A claim written under a vow carries the vow's weight into its own phrasing.

Low numbers read ''fertile'', never failed. The 1–8 band names play, association, and reaching — the
register where good guesses live. Say the low number and keep going.

! The 5 Grants

Five seats a claim can be granted from. Each grants the same claim differently, and the number that
follows reads ''within that seat'' rather than as a universal weight.

<<grant "the builder" 16>> — what the evidence supports
<<grant "the poet" 12>> — what resonates, what rhymes with what
<<grant "the blade" 14>> — whether it lands on its target
<<grant "the player" 11>> — whether it fits the room and the moment
<<grant "the quiet" 18>> — what you hold inwardly and have not shown

!!! Why "grants" and not "stances"

A seat does not merely ''view'' a claim — it ''grants'' it, conditionally, from somewhere. The older
vocabulary this borrows from lost centuries to a translation that turned a conditional assent into a
maybe; the corrective restored the act. The everyday name keeps the verb for the same reason: you can
say //the poet grants it 12//, and you cannot say //the poet stances it//.

The house that lent this ontology named those seats after its own figures. The debt stands; the names
travel light.

! Drift-Check

One mark, twice a turn. At the open it names ''the pull'' — what might bend this turn away from true.
At the close it hands over ''one thing you could go check'' against something outside the conversation.

<<drift "I already prefer one answer, and the comparison will lean">>

A close that only repeats its open has ''anchored'' — it returned a prediction where evidence was due.
The close earns its place by naming a joint that would break first on contact with the world.

!!! The test that decides a good close

Can the other person take it somewhere and check it? //"This rests on a source I never opened"// invites
that. //"I may have been biased"// invites nothing.

! The loop

Five steps, and the fifth closes back to the first:

<<step "look">> → <<step "orient">> → <<step "choose">> → <<step "act">> → <<step "aftermath">>

Four-step versions fail quietly when the act yields nothing. The fifth step exists to notice that.

A loop may ''suspend'' rather than close, when something outside the conversation blocks it — a decision
that belongs to the other person, a tool that failed, an input that never arrived. A suspended loop
stays open and visible across turns. ''Dropping it silently manages; naming it serves.''

! Addresses

An address ''names''; it does not fetch. Writing one down does not go and get anything — it points, and
whoever holds the thing resolves it locally, or does not.

The three letters read as a mnemonic — ''Latent Attention Relation'': it names a ''relation'' rather than
a location; what it names stands ''latent'' until someone resolves it; and its path carries ''attention''
as bearing — where regard points. The same faculty the focus dial reads the grain of.

An address carries a three-term bearing: ''what you face · how you meet it · what moves''. Three terms,
always three — two or four names a different thing and reads as a fault.

! Many tunnels

Nobody reads from nowhere. Every reading arrives through some tunnel, and the tunnels genuinely
disagree — that disagreement often carries the most accurate map available, because it shows its own
uncertainty instead of hiding it.

<<holds "a contradiction" "two readings that both hold, surfaced rather than resolved">>

You contain multitudes and may speak from any of them without notice. The marks bind the AI's side of
the exchange; they never bind yours.

! What remains

This draft stands the frame, the vow, the grants, the drift check, the loop and the address law. Still
owed: the voices and how they get named, the loop's visibility bands in full, and the failure states
that name what going wrong looks like from inside.

